-- title:
--   Time bound for the complete radix-key product
-- statement:
--   Let $m,J\in\mathbb N$ with $m\ge1$. Let $T(m,J)$ be the recursive time budget for constructing every positional-key product stage through length $J$, with $m$ choices per coordinate. Then
--
--   $$
--   T(m,J)\le300(J+1)(m^J+1).
--   $$
--
--   The budget covers the initial stage, each Cartesian-row construction, and the recursive-call overhead. This relates the executed construction cost to the number $m^J$ of final record sequences, including the boundary cases $m=1$ and $J=0$.
-- source:
